: [[" the", -0.4137464463710785], [" `/", -1.2589250802993774]]}, {"t": " default", "lp": -0.7302372455596924, "top": [[" default", -0.7302372455596924], [" multi", -1.1100819110870361]]}, {"t": " `/", "lp": -0.30975207686424255, "top": [[" `/", -0.30975207686424255], [" `", -1.3330751657485962]]}, {"t": "usr", "lp": -0.00013996149937156588, "top": [["usr", -0.00013996149937156588], ["lib", -9.483418464660645]]}, {"t": "/lib", "lp": -0.001441862084902823, "top": [["/lib", -0.001441862084902823], ["/usr", -6.769298553466797]]}, {"t": "6", "lp": -0.005372026469558477, "top": [["6", -0.005372026469558477], ["/c", -5.518265724182129]]}, {"t": "4", "lp": -3.755163197638467e-05, "top": [["4", -3.755163197638467e-05], ["`", -12.15026569366455]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.6849396824836731, "top": [["`", -0.6849396824836731], ["`)", -0.7251713871955872]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're using Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, which aren't on the default PATH.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into broken output.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag by flag:\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` \u2014 **source directory** (where the source code lives)\n- `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` \u2014 **build directory** (where build artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja` \u2014 use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, matches the `ninja` makedepends)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimize for performance (enables `-O3`-level optimizations). This is important because the comment notes CFLAGS leak into the SYCL pipeline, so we control optimization here instead.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install binaries to `/usr`\n- Install libraries to `/usr/lib` (rather than the default `/usr/lib64`"}